# Editor Tools Rules

## Naming
- All tool scripts MUST have the `Tool` suffix in BOTH the class name and the file name.
  - ✅ `GridSpawnerTool` in `GridSpawnerTool.ts`
  - ❌ `GridSpawner` in `GridSpawner.ts`

## Isolation from Main Game Code
- Tools MUST be strictly isolated from the main game codebase.
- FORBIDDEN to import or call Tool classes from `GameBootstrap`, services, gameplay, UI presenters, or any runtime code.
- Tools MUST NOT subscribe to `EventBus`, mutate `GameStore`, or drive the FSM.
- Tools MAY import gameplay types (e.g. `Collectable`, `CollectableType`) only to configure scene objects in the editor.
- Main game code MUST NOT depend on tools — sync results (counts, etc.) go through designer-facing configs like `LevelConfig`, not live tool references.

## Runtime Isolation
- Tools MUST NOT run during gameplay — add this to `onLoad`:

```typescript
onLoad() {
    if (!EDITOR) {
        this.destroy();
        return;
    }
}
```

## Inspector Button Pattern
- All main tool functionality MUST be activated via an inspector button using a get/set property:

```typescript
@property({ tooltip: 'Click to run the tool' })
public get myActionButton(): boolean { return false; }
public set myActionButton(v: boolean) {
    if (v && EDITOR) {
        this.doSomething();
    }
}
```
